# PLAN-852 ace-m1 composite value cases green on the LEGACY engine only
# (observed result == frozen oracle). AC native is scalar-only and the
# AV source profile rejects composite types today — gap/wait rows in
# binding.tsv; they join when their owners deliver. Their a2r-snapshot
# checks compare frozen golden bytes only — the composite emitter output
# is NOT compilable Rust (List<int>.new() pseudo-syntax), so certified-
# run rows for composites stay a registered gap (a2r lowering owner).

```test-case
case {
  schema: "autolang.case/2"
  id: "ace.m1.k01"
  tags: ["ace-m1", "legacy-only"]
  links: ["PLAN-852"]
  source: { file: "src/K01.at", syntax: "auto", path: "main.at" }
  entry: { mode: "program" }
  checks: [
    { id: "autovm", adapter: "avm", action: "run",
      expect: { completion: "success", result: { format: "legacy-display", text: "42" } } },
    { id: "a2r-snapshot", adapter: "a2r", action: "emit", options: { module_name: "m1_k01" },
      expect: { completion: "success", artifacts: [
        { path: "m1_k01.rs", file: "oracle/m1_k01.rs", compare: "bytes" } ] } }
  ]
}
```

